Two separate issues:

**1. `StaticResource` doesn't update at runtime.**
`StaticResource` resolves once at XAML load time. Switch to `DynamicResource` so bindings re-evaluate when you swap the merged dictionary:

```xml
<!-- Instead of this -->
<Label TextColor="{StaticResource PrimaryTextColor}" />

<!-- Use this -->
<Label TextColor="{DynamicResource PrimaryTextColor}" />
```

Then swap themes by replacing the merged dictionary:

```csharp
var mergedDicts = Application.Current.Resources.MergedDictionaries;
mergedDicts.Clear();
mergedDicts.Add(useDark ? new DarkTheme() : new LightTheme());
```

**2. Activity restart on system theme change.**
Android destroys and recreates the Activity when `uiMode` changes. Prevent this by adding `ConfigChanges` to your `MainActivity`:

```csharp
[Activity(Theme = "@style/Maui.SplashTheme", MainLauncher = true,
          ConfigurationChanges = ConfigChanges.ColorMode | ConfigChanges.UiMode
          | ConfigChanges.ScreenSize | ConfigChanges.Orientation)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity { }
```

This tells Android your app handles the config change itself, so it won't restart. You can then detect the change and swap dictionaries:

```csharp
public override void OnConfigurationChanged(Configuration newConfig)
{
    base.OnConfigurationChanged(newConfig);
    bool isDark = (newConfig.UiMode & UiMode.NightMask) == UiMode.NightYes;
    // swap your ResourceDictionary here
}
```

**TL;DR:** `StaticResource` → `DynamicResource` for runtime updates; add `ConfigChanges.UiMode` to prevent the Activity restart.
